   "text": "Why Is Oil So Expensive.\nOil is very important.\nCars, planes, and ships use it.\nFactories use it to make plastic and many other things.\nA lot of the world's oil travels on ships through a narrow sea called the Strait of Hormuz.\nIn normal times, about one fifth of the world's oil goes through it.\nThis year there is a war in the region.\nShips cannot move easily, and an important oil pipeline was attacked.\nWhen less oil can travel, oil becomes more expensive.\nIn October, one barrel of oil cost more than one hundred dollars.\nThat is the highest price in about four years.\nKorea buys almost all of its oil from other countries.\nSo when oil prices go up, Koreans pay more for gas, plane tickets, and even food,\nbecause trucks need fuel to carry it."
